Data notice (not part of the MIT licence above)

This licence covers the source code of El Nino Watch only. The data the
application fetches, stores and displays (ENSO indices, bulletins, forecasts,
buoy measurements, satellite products, disaster alerts, news headlines, social
posts, webcam frames, map tiles, ...) belongs to its providers (NOAA, NASA,
Open-Meteo, Copernicus / ECMWF, the Australian Bureau of Meteorology, JMA, IRI,
WMO, GDACS, the Thai Meteorological Department and the others listed in
docs/DATA_SOURCES.md) and remains under each provider's own terms and licence.
Nothing in this repository grants any right to that data. The test fixtures
under backend/tests/fixtures are small captured samples of those providers'
public responses, kept only so the parsers can be tested offline.

El Nino Watch is not an official warning service. See the "Limitations and
disclaimer" section of README.md.
